{"seq":31,"at":"2026-10-22","kind":"printed","target":{"type":"wording","id":"w24561"},"reason":"Printed on publish-or-perish card pp-019, category 2; the card's own words are kept in cardText — \"[Religious Studies] What is a mezuzah?\nA. A prayer shawl\nB. A scroll containing biblical verses\nC. A ceremonial cup\nAnswer: B. A mezuzah contains parchment inscribed with verses from the Torah. It’s placed inside a decorative case and affixed to the doorframes of many Jewish people’s homes. Many Jewish people touch or kiss the mezuzah when passing through the doorway as a sign of respect and devotion.\".","by":"merge art/architecture, art/design, art/painting, art/sculpture, belief/philosophy, belief/religion, belief/symbols, ear","ref":"quiz-archive/transcripts/publish-or-perish/pp-019.json","changes":[{"field":"en","new":"What is the name of the parchment inscribed with Torah verses that Jews place in a small case on the doorposts of their homes, and often touch or kiss when passing through?"},{"field":"de","new":"Wie heißt das mit Versen aus der Tora beschriftete Pergament, das Juden in einer kleinen Kapsel am Türpfosten ihrer Wohnungen anbringen und beim Durchgehen oft berühren oder küssen?"},{"field":"origin","new":"printed"},{"field":"printed","new":{"source":"publish-or-perish","card":"pp-019","category":2}},{"field":"cardText","diff":[["+","[Religious Studies] What is a mezuzah?\nA. A prayer shawl\nB. A scroll containing biblical verses\nC. A ceremonial cup\nAnswer: B. A mezuzah contains parchment inscribed with verses from the Torah. It’s placed inside a decorative case and affixed to the doorframes of many Jewish people’s homes. Many Jewish people touch or kiss the mezuzah when passing through the doorway as a sign of respect and devotion."]]},{"field":"fact","new":"f03940"}],"hash":"433e0362b80d"},
